# No issue / PR numbers in the repo

Do **not** cite GitHub issues, pull requests, or tracker IDs in committed content.

## Forbidden in

- Source code (comments, rustdoc, docstrings, string literals used as docs)
- Docs (`docs/`, `.agents/docs/`, plan/solution/brainstorm artifacts)
- READMEs and other markdown at any path
- Compose/env examples, AGENTS.md, cursor rules (except this rule)

## Forbidden forms

- `issue #62`, `#62`, `Issue 27`, `(issue #53)`
- Links like `https://github.com/.../issues/62` or `.../pull/12`
- Headings such as `## Commerce landings (issue #62)`
- “See #10”, “for #55”, “parent #13”, “closes #8”, “umbrella #10”

Tracker IDs belong in GitHub (issue bodies, PR descriptions, project boards)—not in the tree.

## Allowed

- Describe the **product/work** without a number (“encrypted entitlements store”, “commerce landings”)
- Link to **durable repo docs** (`docs/one-cvm-architecture.md`, `site/README.md`)
- Upstream library docs that are not issue/PR pages (API swagger, crates.io, etc.)

```text
# BAD
/// Encrypted entitlements (issue #53).
## Commerce landings (issue #62)
See [issue #10](https://github.com/BreadchainCoop/sigstack-bot/issues/10).

# GOOD
/// Encrypted entitlements store; CRUD for future webhook / !link / gating.
## Commerce landings
See [docs/one-cvm-architecture.md](docs/one-cvm-architecture.md).
```

When editing existing files, strip leftover issue/PR citations rather than leaving them.
